WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.012
COALESCE returns the first non-null expression.

00:00:03.012 --> 00:00:09.837
Here, we try cleaned email first, then cleaned phone, then a text label saying no contact method.

00:00:09.837 --> 00:00:13.252
This is a reporting or business-logic fallback.

00:00:13.252 --> 00:00:16.272
It does not repair the missing email or phone.

00:00:16.272 --> 00:00:22.342
The source still has the same missingness; we are simply choosing a value for the current output.

00:00:22.342 --> 00:00:27.372
Missingness has several representations: NULL, blank text, whitespace,

00:00:27.372 --> 00:00:31.082
and sometimes sentinel codes such as Unknown or 999.

00:00:31.082 --> 00:00:32.517
Do not collapse them blindly.

00:00:32.517 --> 00:00:37.987
First decide whether they mean the same thing in the source system,

00:00:37.987 --> 00:00:42.706
then normalize deliberately and keep lineage when the original value may matter.
